    },
    "message": "Move the rules of the overlay, temporary spaces and independent queues to Rust\n\nrules/overlay.rs takes domain/temporary_spaces.py and the rules of\ndomain/geometry_overlay.py: capacity, beds and room intake, placing an\ninstalled facility, checking and applying an approved floor-plan change, and\nthe state's check. events/effects.py's handlers call these directly. The sleep\nbranch of _apply_effect now plans a bed.\n\nfacility_queues_v1 gets a typed row, and rules/facility_queues.rs its rules. The\nqueue, movement and service kernels take a queue_id instead of refusing it.\nResults do not change: the Python rules stay the comparison base.\n\nGeo builds the effective plan itself and holds the service points.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
